<title>AUSTRIA: Indonesia coffee crop seen down 25-30 pct.</title>
<headline>Indonesia coffee crop seen down 25-30 pct.</headline>
<dateline>VIENNA 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The association of Indonesian coffee exporters said on Wednesday it expected the country's coffee crop to drop by at least 25 percent this year.</p>
<p>&quot;This year the crop will be smaller because of weather problems. We have had too much rain and heavy winds through the flowering period which has damaged the production. We expect it to be approximately 25 to 30 percent down from last year,&quot; Mansyur Tandiono, chairman of the association of Indonesian coffee exporters, told Reuters during the Second International Coffee and Tea Symposium conference in the Austrian capital.</p>
<p>Last year Indonesia had a total production of 500,000 tonnes of coffee, of which 380,000 tonnes were exported.</p>
</text>
